    "turn_text": "And we made it clear doing the regular session that we did not want to deal with the Constitution. at that time and we did not do not want to deal with it for the remainder of this year. And so it may be news to some, but many legislators have always felt that there was no need for a constitutional convention. And the constitutional convention, when I was in a legislature, was a big big challenge. The bill actually came before my committee, and we held it in committee because we got a consensus from the members of the Senate, and the members of the Senate said, listen, if that's what you want to do, do it, and that's what I did. I held it in committee. And we have enough to fight about it at this stage in our lives. And the Constitution is, I think, there are some merits to making the Constitution smaller. There are some things that are in the Constitution that perhaps, in my view, shouldn't be in the",
