    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48043.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "No, you're not wrong. It wouldn't take a year, but it did take a year in 73, as it was. But it certainly would take more than two weeks. And what they wanted to do, they wanted to decide all the issues before we went into the convention and decide to delegates and then go in and then rush the convention in two weeks. Most of us in the Senate just said, that's just not wise. We can't do it. Now, on the House side, and have the utmost respect, for all of my house members, they pass resolutions, pass resolutions to say, we're not going to deal with MFP, we're not going. But that really doesn't have any merits once you have the convention. Everything is open. And so we need to have a very clear and we need to have the right delegates. Here's another problem we had passed. There was some on the Senate side, me being one of them, didn't feel that it was balanced. I mean, to put the House in the Senate, to make them delegates and then give the governor 27 people, you can't make my vote equal to a House member",
