    "turn_text": "I mean, I understand when you go to Congress and you work hard and you move up in the leadership, and then at the end of the day, you just have a district just wiped from under you, not by the vote of the people, but by the vote of the courts. That happened to me, 27 years ago. So I do understand his pain. But at the end of the day, But we have this document called the Voting Rights Act. And states no matter how they don't like, how much they don't like it, they have to comply with it. Now, we don't have subsection five, which was easier back in the",
