    "turn_text": "at a very early age. One of the things I wanted to do this term, last term, is I wanted to make a kindergarten mandatory. I was chairman of education. And Senator Peacock, who was since disease, he was chairman of education when I was back in the Senate years ago. And he started fighting for that issue, and it never, you know, the members never opened their minds to it. And so I was able to do it. I got members of the House and the Senate, and we worked as a coalition. And now, I mean, can I go in this mandatory? Now, why did I do that? Why did I do that? I did it because... Actually, a kindergarten is too late, but it must be",
