    "turn_text": "prisons and incarcerating people because what we do in Louisiana now, we test the kid when they get third grade and they say they're reading below grade level and then we want to say the education system is not doing their job one and a half. charter schools and they're failing because we failed them. I believe in investing in children early and you get better results. When little Johnny can't read at the third grade, he don't want to go to class. And it's not that he has something against education. He doesn't want to be different. I can't read everybody else's reading. And the only reason why a little Johnny can't read is because he had no pre-K and he probably had no kindergarten. And we got to do a better job at that as a state.",
