    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48043.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 80,
    "turn_text": "You know, pay, you know, and look, we're moving up that ladder. I'm one of the individuals who has the ability to pay teachers more. So don't get on this talking about pay teachers more. You there. We have improved teachers, however. We have fights every day, this past session. was session before last, I wanted to make the $2,000 per minute. We did it as a tip, the legislation. I fought that, fought it very hard because I mean, you know, you can't say our schools are failing and we don't want to even deal with the engine of the schools, the teachers, the people were there to teach the kids. But we failed that fight. We were able to give them tip, but every year we got to approve it. This compensation, additional compensation. The legislature in the state, we have to be committed to education and public education. And until we are, we're going to continue to have the same results. It's not going to change. We've got to have a commitment to public education Right now, people want to take public dollars and use it for charter schools, and I just think that's count up",
