    "turn_text": "to get ready to go and fight on Monday. And that's the challenges we all have. You know, that progressive keep fighting, you know, don't lose no hope. You know, you are the future. I mean, you shape the future. You decide, you know, and look, people got to put, you know, I'll be the first to tell people. Politics is not the only battle to fight. We got to have our share of people elected because those are decision makers. We got to have our share of judges because when we are up, we got to make sure that we got to see some system that looks somewhat like us, you know, a school board, the whole works. But then there's some other stuff that every individual has to have to do. You know, it takes a village to raise a child when you see somebody doing drugs, doing whatever, you know, you try to deal with it, call their mother, call their father, go to college, you know, and become a professional. Everybody's not going to do that. Go to trade school, you know, make something of your life, no matter what it is. I mean, we all have kind of a personal responsibility. But don't put all of that hope in, if I elect this guy's judge, all the problems are going to go away. If I elect this guy as the congressman. We're not going to have the minimum wage battle. He's going to fix it",
