    "turn_text": "think that it's where media comes into play, to a large extent. Media has changed over my lifetime. The advent of cable. When I was a kid, it was the 530 National News on one of the three major stations, CBS, NBC, ABC, and then the six o'clock local news. And that was it. Now you have CNN, you have Fox, you have... News Nation, you have Newsmax, you have my personal favorite MSNBC, but all of them are partisan. And they promote an idea of highlighting a particular perspective. And in highlighting their perspective, they want to denigrate the opposite perspective. And they want to point fingers of blame at other people. Those Democrats got into office, but they can't do anything. They can't leave. That's why you needed to make a different kind of vote. And it has an impact on this generation of people, because what I find is they don't read. And they don't avail themselves to a wide array of opinions. I was sitting with a young man yesterday, smart young man, fine young man, man-rable young man. I asked him, do you read the newspaper? No. Do you read books? No. So if you don't read, if you don't expose yourself to anything, then you are wide open to being influenced by media that says those people are responsible for your plight",
