    "turn_text": "it becomes a revolving, you know, so I'm not supporting that. And I know that there's some Democrats who are who are thinking about pushing such a measure. I'm just not for that. I hadn't heard of any other measures as related to the Supreme Court, but you're right. I mean, that as always, when we couldn't depend on anything else, we were always able to depend on the courts. You know, look at all of the important decisions throughout, you know, past history. It's all Brown v. Board of Education, all these important issues, it was the court. I think that's going to change. You know, everybody has a season. You know, there's a season and there would be a season for justice for lack of an analogy. And that season is coming. I'm hopeful that Kamala gets elected, there's a possibility of having two justices retire, and she would have the opportunity to appoint both. So, seasons, and that's why I tell people, you know, even some of my colleagues who I, who I have most respect for, you know, like fighting for this, these majority black districts. I would say to them now, if you were in the minority and you made up 33% of the population, then you only had one of six. Would you be fighting? And every time, I mean, without any, yes, I would be, I understand. And everybody understand what I'm fighting for, but, you know, very few people want to fight with me. And it took a while. You got to just keep working it, keep working it, keep working it. And finally, God, now some had other, you know, other reasons for doing what they did, but at the end of the day, we got them all on the same page. This is wrong. It's absolutely wrong. It has to be fixed. And it's just a constant battle. I don't know why. I think I know why, but it's just a constant battle. Equality in my view has always been a good word. You know, now is a bad word. I mean, I just don't get it. Diversity, in my view, has always been a good word.",
