    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48043.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 167,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, I mean, look, I mean, we need to cease fire. I mean, how we get there, I don't know, but you cannot, I mean, you know, you cannot keep killing innocent people. It's, I mean, I think Vice President Harris spoke to it. I mean, you know, Israel is one of our big allies, as we all know, but at the end of the day, you know, we have to give some stability to the situation in the Middle East whereby we can operate with more restraint. I mean, just because we have the power to kill the power, doesn't mean that we have to. And I think Netanyahu has to operate with a little bit more restraint. And I think he sensed that in the past couple of days he's been in DC. I think that the leadership has basically said to him what I just said. And people don't want to turn on their TV and see a whole bunch of kids, babies, dying in the streets for no good reason.",
